1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Okay, moving into congenital defects.

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:04,560
These usually arise during embryogenesis,

3
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:07,000
classically during weeks three to eight.

4
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:09,440
They're seen in about 1% of live births,

5
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,980
and most of these are sporadic.

6
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:14,080
They can occur in association with certain circumstances.

7
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:16,240
That becomes particularly high yield,

8
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,900
but I'll mention those associations as we go forward.

9
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:21,200
Now, one of the interesting things that can occur

10
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,500
when you get congenital defects

11
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,100
is that you get shunting between the circulations,

12
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,000
whether it be left to right or right to left.

13
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:29,740
I'll highlight some of these principles as we move forward.

14
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:31,200
Let's start with the first defect.

15
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:33,300
So in ventricular septal defect,

16
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:34,960
you get a defect in the septum

17
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:36,840
that divides the right and left ventricles.

18
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:39,540
Of course, the name gives it away, ventricular septal defect.

19
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:40,760
Important to note,

20
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:43,340
this is the most common congenital heart defect,

21
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:47,960
and very high yield is associated with fetal alcohol syndrome.

22
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:49,880
Now, let's just illustrate the anatomy

23
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,220
to understand the problem.

24
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:54,920
So here you've got the right atrium and the right ventricle,

25
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,220
and then, of course, you've got the left atrium

26
00:00:58,220 --> 00:00:59,700
and the left ventricle.

27
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:01,560
And the defect is going to be here

28
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:04,140
in between the right and left ventricles.

29
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:06,040
Now, when blood comes from the right atrium

30
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:08,300
into the right ventricle, there'll be no problem.

31
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:09,600
From the right ventricle,

32
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:11,620
it can choose to go into the left ventricle,

33
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:13,100
which would be a high-pressure circuit,

34
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,900
or stay in the low-pressure circuit,

35
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:17,000
and so it'll continue on through the low-pressure circuit.

36
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:20,280
Eventually, blood will return to the left atrium,

37
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:22,180
and when blood gets to the left atrium,

38
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:23,540
it'll enter the left ventricle.

39
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:24,780
From the left ventricle,

40
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:27,520
it can choose to proceed in the high-pressure circuit

41
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:29,300
of the systemic circulation

42
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:31,740
or cross over into the low-pressure circuit

43
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:33,000
of the pulmonary circulation,

44
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:34,660
and so you'll get some crossover,

45
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:36,720
and that crossover is going to result

46
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:38,900
in a left-to-right shunt,

47
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:41,640
and that's the key problem in VSD.

48
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:44,140
Now, if this VSD is small,

49
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:45,980
then it can be relatively asymptomatic.

50
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:47,860
However, if the VSD is large,

51
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:49,760
then large amounts of blood would cross over.

52
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:52,340
Now, when that large amounts of blood crosses over,

53
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:54,520
that's going to increase the blood volume

54
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:56,080
within the pulmonary circuit.

55
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:58,740
The increase in blood volume within the pulmonary circuit

56
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:00,960
will eventually result in pulmonary hypertension,

57
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:02,780
so you'll get a high blood pressure

58
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:04,340
within the pulmonary circuit,

59
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,140
and eventually what'll happen is that

60
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:08,000
as blood crosses over the right atrium

61
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,120
into the right ventricle,

62
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:11,920
there'll be a choice to go into the high-pressure circuit

63
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:15,180
of the pulmonary circuit because there's hypertension,

64
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:17,720
or cross back over into the low-pressure circuit,

65
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:19,160
and eventually the time will come

66
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:21,080
when it's actually better to cross over

67
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:24,740
into the relatively lower-pressure systemic circuit.

68
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:26,720
And so then what will eventually happen

69
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:28,660
is you'll get reversal of the shunt

70
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:30,900
so that you now get a right-to-left shunt,

71
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,640
and when you get reversal of the shunt,

72
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:33,840
you're going to get blue blood,

73
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:36,060
which is coming from the right side

74
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:38,720
into the left systemic circuit,

75
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:40,740
which will then result in cyanosis.

76
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:43,320
Now, this has been explained in your text

77
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,040
in words as well,

78
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,820
where I say that there's a left-to-right shunt,

79
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:48,740
the size of the defect determines the extent of shunting

80
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,100
and the age of presentation.

81
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:52,180
Small defects are asymptomatic,

82
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:54,540
and large defects can result in Eisenmenger's syndrome.

83
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:56,720
Now, again, when you get Eisenmenger's syndrome,

84
00:02:56,820 --> 00:02:58,140
there's some important consequences.

85
00:02:58,340 --> 00:02:59,600
For example, the patient will have

86
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:00,880
right ventricular hypertrophy.

87
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:01,220
Why?

88
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,340
Because the right ventricle is now pumping

89
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:04,620
against a much higher pressure.

90
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,100
You can get polycythemia

91
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:08,160
because as you get deoxygenated blood

92
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:10,620
coming across into the systemic circuit,

93
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:12,800
that's then going to result in hypoxemia,

94
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:15,580
and therefore, you'll get release of erythropoietin,

95
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:17,600
which will then result in polycythemia.

96
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:19,380
And finally, you can get clubbing,

97
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,300
and clubbing is a change in the fingernails

98
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:22,780
due to the cyanosis.

99
00:03:23,340 --> 00:03:24,680
The treatment is surgical closure

100
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:25,600
for a large defect.

101
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:28,340
Small defects may close spontaneously.

102
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:30,100
An atrial septal defect

103
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:32,340
is when you get a defect in the septa

104
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:34,080
that divides the left and right atria.

105
00:03:34,580 --> 00:03:37,020
The most common type is called osteum secundum.

106
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:39,340
However, there's an osteum primum type,

107
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:41,160
and that's associated with Down syndrome,

108
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,540
which is very high yield.

109
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:45,060
This results in a left-to-right shunt

110
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:47,760
with a split S2 on auscultation.

111
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,200
Now, the idea here,

112
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:50,380
if you go back to the anatomy,

113
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,860
is that you've got the right atrium,

114
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,100
you've got the right ventricle,

115
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,080
the left atrium, and the left ventricle,

116
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,860
and, of course, the defect is here

117
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:57,900
in between the atria.

118
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,420
Now, what's going to happen

119
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:02,320
is that blood from the high-pressure circuit

120
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,260
on the left side

121
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:05,600
will cross over into the lower-pressure circuit

122
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:06,460
on the right side.

123
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:08,180
And as that blood crosses over,

124
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:09,700
you're going to be putting extra volume

125
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:10,800
onto the right side,

126
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,920
and that extra volume on the right side

127
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,840
will result in a delayed closure

128
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,220
of the pulmonic valve.

129
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,680
Now, that delayed closure of the pulmonary valve

130
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,480
in relation to the aortic valve

131
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:22,960
will result in a splitting of the S2,

132
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:24,060
and, of course, the S2

133
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:26,500
is when the aortic and the pulmonic valve close.

134
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:28,140
Another interesting finding

135
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:29,260
of an atrial septal defect

136
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:31,720
is that if you happen to have a DVT,

137
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:32,880
for example, down here,

138
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:35,760
and that DVT were to break off and embolize,

139
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,880
normally it would go up into the right circuit

140
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:40,120
and eventually make its way into the lung,

141
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:42,340
resulting in a pulmonary embolus.

142
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:44,660
However, because in this particular case

143
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:45,520
you've got an ASD,

144
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,620
it is possible for that embolus

145
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,500
to cross over onto the left side,

146
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,500
and when it crosses over into the left side,

147
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:53,160
it could then go through the systemic circuit

148
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,260
and lodge, for example, in the brain

149
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:57,440
or in the distal extremities.

150
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:00,300
And so that is called a paradoxical embolus

151
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,060
because you get an embolus

152
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:04,260
that arises from the right side

153
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:05,760
but then crosses over

154
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,340
to lodge on the left side.

155
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:09,720
Patent ductus arteriosus arises

156
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:11,980
when there's failure of the ductus arteriosus

157
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:14,000
to close, and very high yield

158
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,420
is associated with congenital rubella.

159
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,140
Now, again, if you understand the anatomy,

160
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:19,440
things become very straightforward.

161
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:21,620
So let's just briefly illustrate this.

162
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:22,960
Here's the right atrium,

163
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:24,700
and then you've got the right ventricle.

164
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,480
Of course, this is all normal,

165
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:27,840
and you've got the left atrium

166
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:29,060
and the left ventricle.

167
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:32,040
Now, coming off the right ventricle

168
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,180
is the pulmonary artery,

169
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:36,080
and coming off the left ventricle

170
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,540
is going to be the aorta.

171
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:39,540
Now, immediately coming off the aorta

172
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:41,920
will be the major branches at the arch,

173
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:43,320
so we'll make those here.

174
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,940
And then recall that the PDA

175
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:46,920
connects the pulmonary artery with the aorta

176
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,040
after those major branches come off.

177
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:51,060
So now what's going to happen in this case

178
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:52,340
is you're going to go from the right atrium

179
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:53,320
to the right ventricle,

180
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:55,200
from the right ventricle to the pulmonary circuit,

181
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,620
and in the pulmonary circuit,

182
00:05:56,700 --> 00:05:58,080
you'll have a choice to cross over

183
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,420
into the high-pressure aorta

184
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:01,740
or continue down into the pulmonary circuit.

185
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:03,980
Of course, you'll continue down,

186
00:06:04,380 --> 00:06:06,220
and then eventually blood will come around

187
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:07,980
from the left atrium to the left ventricle,

188
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,380
from the left ventricle to the aorta,

189
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:10,940
and eventually that will lead

190
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:12,320
to the crossing over of blood

191
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:14,740
from the aorta to the pulmonary circuit.

192
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,660
Now what's going to happen over time

193
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:18,760
is that as you increase blood volume over here,

194
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:20,760
you're going to create pulmonary hypertension.

195
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:23,640
This pulmonary hypertension will eventually result

196
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:24,800
in reversal of the shunt.

197
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,520
So that blood will eventually cross over this way.

198
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:29,340
When blood crosses over this way,

199
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:31,420
you're going to have deoxygenated blood

200
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:33,440
or blue blood crossing over,

201
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:35,680
and that blue blood is going to go

202
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,800
into the lower extremities

203
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:39,020
because here this was going to the upper extremity.

204
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,900
So now you're going to get cyanosis

205
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,360
in a lower extremity later in life,

206
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:45,320
and that's particularly high yield.

207
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,280
And so again, we say for the PDA

208
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:48,980
that you're going to have a left to right shunt,

209
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:50,980
it's asymptomatic at birth,

210
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:52,160
but it's going to be associated

211
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,760
with a holosystolic machine-like murmur.

212
00:06:55,340 --> 00:06:56,820
If you get Eisenmenger's syndrome,

213
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:58,320
which would be reversal of the shunt,

214
00:06:58,620 --> 00:07:01,380
that's going to result in lower extremity cyanosis,

215
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,680
and that's because the PDA arises

216
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:06,360
after the major branches off the aortic arch.

217
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,360
So this is particularly high yield.

218
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:10,220
The treatment is indomethacin,

219
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:12,000
and the idea is that indomethacin

220
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,660
decreases prostaglandin E,

221
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:17,520
and prostaglandin E is what keeps the PDA open.

222
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:20,500
Prostaglandin E keeps the PDA open.

223
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:21,460
And so therefore,

224
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:25,020
removal of prostaglandin E will close the PDA.

225
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:28,040
The next disorder is tetralogy of flow,

226
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:29,560
and when you have tetralogy of flow,

227
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:30,840
there's going to be four problems,

228
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,260
and if you understand the anatomy,

229
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,840
it makes it particularly easy

230
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:35,360
to understand what's going to happen.

231
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:37,120
So let's go back to the whiteboard

232
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,420
and simply draw our diagram.

233
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:39,820
You've got the right atrium,

234
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,160
the right ventricle,

235
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:42,400
the left atrium,

236
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:43,720
and the left ventricle.

237
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:44,720
Now again,

238
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:46,840
the key problem here

239
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:47,920
is going to be number one,

240
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:49,060
you're going to have a stenosis

241
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:50,620
of the pulmonary outflow tract.

242
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:51,560
Number two,

243
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,600
there will be a VSD.

244
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:53,740
Number three,

245
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:56,780
the aorta will be overriding that VSD.

246
00:07:57,220 --> 00:07:57,880
And number four,

247
00:07:57,980 --> 00:07:59,420
you'll have right ventricular hypertrophy.

248
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:01,600
So these are some of the key findings.

249
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:03,120
Now when blood tries to go

250
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:03,840
from the right atrium

251
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:04,740
to the right ventricle,

252
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,440
no problem.

253
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:06,780
From the right ventricle,

254
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:08,620
because there is a stenosis,

255
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:09,860
we're going to get shunting

256
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:11,140
down into the aorta,

257
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:12,520
which is then going to result

258
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:14,640
in a right to left shunt.

259
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:15,880
And so the key finding

260
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:17,140
is that these will be babies

261
00:08:17,140 --> 00:08:18,020
that will be born,

262
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:20,440
and they will become cyanotic

263
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:22,000
because deoxygenated blood

264
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,180
is going into the left

265
00:08:24,180 --> 00:08:25,480
or systemic circuit.

266
00:08:25,780 --> 00:08:27,320
So you get early cyanosis.

267
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:28,280
Now of course,

268
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:29,400
the degree of shunting

269
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:30,720
is all going to be based

270
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,480
on this stenosis.

271
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:33,140
If this stenosis is really tight,

272
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,020
you'll get more shunting,

273
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:35,840
and if the stenosis is loose,

274
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:36,800
you'll get less shunting.

275
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,380
Now one of the interesting things

276
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:39,080
about these patients

277
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:40,080
is that they can become

278
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:40,900
very cyanotic,

279
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:42,060
especially during exercise.

280
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,600
And so they'll run around,

281
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:44,500
run around, run around,

282
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:45,860
and become severely cyanotic.

283
00:08:46,220 --> 00:08:47,260
And then what they'll do

284
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:48,400
in order to reverse

285
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,380
the cyanotic spell

286
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:50,840
is that they'll squat down.

287
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:52,080
When they squat down,

288
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,400
they're basically increasing

289
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,780
the pressure on this side,

290
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:56,140
and that increased pressure

291
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,540
will decrease the shunt,

292
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,940
sending more blood to the lung.

293
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:00,240
And when they send more blood

294
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:00,780
to the lung,

295
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:02,180
they will then be able to,

296
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:03,540
again, oxygenate that blood

297
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:05,100
and become less cyanotic.

298
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:06,800
And that's an important physiology

299
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:08,300
to understand in this disorder.

300
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:10,440
So we say that tetralogy of flow

301
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:11,880
gives you a right-to-left shunt,

302
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:13,320
giving early cyanosis,

303
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:15,240
and the degree of stenosis

304
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,420
determines the extent

305
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:17,780
of the shunting and cyanosis.

306
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:20,540
In response to cyanotic spells,

307
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:21,740
patients will squat.

308
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:22,880
That will increase

309
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,840
the arterial vascular resistance,

310
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:26,260
which will decrease the shunt

311
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:27,920
and send more blood to the lungs.

312
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:29,760
Now one of the classic findings

313
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:32,560
will be this boot-shaped heart on X-ray.

314
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,380
So this kind of looks like a little boot,

315
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,100
and that's particularly high yield,

316
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,740
the boot-shaped heart on X-ray.

317
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:39,000
The next disorder

318
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,760
is transposition of the great vessels.

319
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:41,900
The anatomy here

320
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:42,580
is very straightforward,

321
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:43,900
so let's just explain it.

322
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:46,180
Right atrium, right ventricle,

323
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:48,500
left atrium, left ventricle.

324
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,860
Transposition means that the aorta

325
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,160
will come off the right side,

326
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,920
and the pulmonary trunk

327
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,060
will come off the left side.

328
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:56,140
Now you can imagine,

329
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:58,200
right atrium to right ventricle to aorta,

330
00:09:58,200 --> 00:09:59,900
the aorta eventually goes

331
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:00,920
through the systemic circuit

332
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:02,440
and drains back into the right atrium.

333
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,580
So you're going to create a circle here.

334
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:05,960
And then left atrium

335
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,760
to left ventricle to pulmonary circuit,

336
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,220
of course the pulmonary circuit

337
00:10:09,220 --> 00:10:10,820
eventually drains into the left atrium.

338
00:10:11,140 --> 00:10:11,800
So you're going to create

339
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:13,020
a separate circuit here.

340
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:14,560
So this is going to result

341
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:16,160
in two independent circuits

342
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:17,300
that do not mix.

343
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:18,620
And the only way

344
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:19,920
that the baby will be able

345
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:21,060
to survive after birth

346
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:23,100
is for us to create an opening

347
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,220
between these circuits.

348
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:25,620
Now one way that you can create

349
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:27,580
that opening is to maintain the PDA,

350
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:29,060
and so we can, for example,

351
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:30,680
give prostaglandin E,

352
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:33,840
which keeps open the PDA.

353
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,400
So let's go ahead and read now.

354
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:37,040
Transposition of the great vessels.

355
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:38,440
So you get the pulmonary artery

356
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,880
arising from the left ventricle,

357
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,520
the aorta from the right ventricle,

358
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:42,640
as I've already described.

359
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,880
Associated with maternal diabetes.

360
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:45,800
High yield.

361
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:47,400
High yield that this is associated

362
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:48,860
with maternal diabetes.

363
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:50,480
This is going to present

364
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,580
with early cyanosis,

365
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:53,220
and that's because the blood

366
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:54,900
from the right side of the heart

367
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,040
is basically going to go

368
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:56,780
into the aorta,

369
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:57,700
and then it's going to go

370
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:58,720
back into the right side

371
00:10:58,720 --> 00:10:59,080
of the heart

372
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,180
and back into the aorta,

373
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:02,760
and that'll all be deoxygenated blood

374
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:03,960
running through the circuit.

375
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,360
Again, we know that

376
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,400
the circuits do not mix.

377
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:07,500
In order for the baby

378
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:08,720
to survive after birth,

379
00:11:08,780 --> 00:11:09,220
we're going to need

380
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:10,080
to create a shunt,

381
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:11,400
and one way we can do that

382
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:12,740
is to give prostaglandin E,

383
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:14,920
which will maintain the PDA

384
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,520
until we can eventually

385
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:18,140
surgically repair this problem.

386
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:19,640
Truncus arteriosus

387
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:21,380
is when you have one large trunk

388
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:23,200
arising from both ventricles,

389
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:26,020
and it fails to divide.

390
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:27,380
So here's the idea.

391
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,340
We've got our standard

392
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:30,500
right atrium, right ventricle,

393
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:32,760
left atrium, left ventricle,

394
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,360
and the idea here is that

395
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,320
you've got this large trunk

396
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,740
coming off both ventricles.

397
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:38,480
Now, of course,

398
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:39,660
this will eventually divide

399
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:40,780
into the pulmonary circuit,

400
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:42,260
and this will eventually divide

401
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:43,540
into the aorta.

402
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:45,180
However, what's going to happen

403
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:46,620
is that the deoxygenated blood

404
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:47,420
coming from here

405
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:48,600
is going to mix

406
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:49,760
with the oxygenated blood

407
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:50,420
coming here,

408
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:51,600
so that you're going to send

409
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:52,960
some deoxygenated blood

410
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,040
down this way,

411
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:55,360
and it's going to result

412
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,780
in early cyanosis.

413
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:58,360
And so these patients

414
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,800
present with early cyanosis,

415
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:00,540
and the reason is

416
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:01,760
that the deoxygenated blood

417
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:02,800
from the right ventricle

418
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:04,900
mixes with the oxygenated blood

419
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:05,860
from the left ventricle

420
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:07,180
before those circuits

421
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:07,980
actually separate.

422
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:09,080
I've already described that

423
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:09,940
in the image.

424
00:12:10,740 --> 00:12:11,780
Tricuspid atresia

425
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:13,460
is when the tricuspid valve

426
00:12:13,460 --> 00:12:14,820
orifice fails to develop,

427
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:15,520
and again,

428
00:12:15,620 --> 00:12:16,720
the word atresia means

429
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:17,940
that you fail to form

430
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,780
the lumen of a tube,

431
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:20,980
and in this particular case,

432
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:22,340
the tube is the atrium.

433
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:23,320
Now, basically,

434
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:24,260
what's going to happen here

435
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:24,980
is the following.

436
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:26,340
You've got the right atrium,

437
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:27,660
right ventricle,

438
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:28,660
left atrium,

439
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:29,740
left ventricle,

440
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:30,900
and of course,

441
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:31,440
this is where

442
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,580
the tricuspid valve is,

443
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:34,400
so if this fails to form,

444
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:35,560
then you're not going

445
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:36,440
to be sending blood

446
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,160
into the right ventricle.

447
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:38,900
So, of course,

448
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:39,980
in response to that,

449
00:12:40,060 --> 00:12:40,860
the right ventricle

450
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:41,780
is going to become

451
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:43,080
hypoplastic.

452
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:44,400
Now, this is classically

453
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:45,940
associated with an ASD,

454
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:46,900
so that there would be

455
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:47,680
an opening here,

456
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:48,600
and that opening

457
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:49,380
would allow blood

458
00:12:49,380 --> 00:12:50,400
to cross over.

459
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:52,180
Now, this baby

460
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:52,780
is going to present

461
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:53,880
with early cyanosis,

462
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:54,540
and that's because

463
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:55,680
the blood from the right side

464
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:56,240
is going to move

465
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:56,960
to the left side,

466
00:12:57,260 --> 00:12:57,720
and so you're going

467
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,860
to get the deoxygenated

468
00:12:58,860 --> 00:12:59,860
blue blood going

469
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:01,040
into the systemic circuit,

470
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:03,040
creating early cyanosis.

471
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:04,920
Coarctation of the aorta

472
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:05,520
is when you have

473
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:06,680
narrowing of the aorta,

474
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:07,660
and it's divided

475
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:08,620
into two forms,

476
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:10,240
infantile and adult forms.

477
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:11,300
Here's a picture

478
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,340
of coarctation,

479
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:12,980
and you can see here

480
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:13,820
is the normal aorta

481
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:14,600
coming off the heart,

482
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:15,640
and all of a sudden,

483
00:13:15,780 --> 00:13:16,920
there's this narrowing

484
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:17,820
of the aorta,

485
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:18,700
and that's called

486
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:19,640
a coarctation.

487
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,580
Now, in the infantile form,

488
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:22,580
it's associated

489
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:23,540
with the PDA,

490
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,740
and the coarctation occurs

491
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:26,900
just distal

492
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:28,160
to the aortic arch,

493
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:29,440
but proximal

494
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:30,120
to the PDA.

495
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:31,340
Let's illustrate that.

496
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:32,080
So here,

497
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:32,680
it's giving you

498
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:33,500
standard anatomy.

499
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:35,280
You've got the right atrium,

500
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:36,460
the right ventricle,

501
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:37,580
the left atrium,

502
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:39,340
and the left ventricle.

503
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:40,340
Now, basically,

504
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:41,080
the idea here

505
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:41,700
is that you've got

506
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:42,320
the aorta,

507
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:42,920
and of course,

508
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,120
you've got the major branches

509
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,240
coming off the aorta,

510
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:47,800
and then you've got a PDA.

511
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,160
So the PDA, of course,

512
00:13:49,220 --> 00:13:49,640
would connect

513
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:50,620
to the pulmonary circuit.

514
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:52,540
Now, the coarctation

515
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:53,900
is going to be here.

516
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:54,680
So there's going to be

517
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:55,560
a tightening here.

518
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:56,660
Now, let's follow blood

519
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:57,880
in this particular circumstance.

520
00:13:58,400 --> 00:13:58,800
Blood will go

521
00:13:58,800 --> 00:13:59,560
from the right atrium

522
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:00,600
to the right ventricle,

523
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:01,840
from the right ventricle

524
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,120
into the pulmonary trunk,

525
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:04,480
and from the pulmonary trunk,

526
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:05,980
some of the deoxygenated blood

527
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:07,060
will actually cross over

528
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:07,720
and come here

529
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:09,280
because this block

530
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:11,640
is making what's beyond it

531
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:12,360
low pressure.

532
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,700
So because you're going

533
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:14,380
to have low pressure

534
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:15,240
behind the block

535
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,480
or beyond the block,

536
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:17,460
you're going to get blood

537
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:18,360
crossing over here.

538
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:19,100
And so you're going

539
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,400
to get some blue

540
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:21,500
deoxygenated blood

541
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:22,980
going to the lower extremity,

542
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:23,640
and these babies

543
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:24,340
are going to present

544
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:26,820
with lower extremity cyanosis.

545
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:28,000
So let's go back

546
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:28,700
and read what we say

547
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:29,820
about the infantile form.

548
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:30,820
It's associated

549
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:31,680
with a PDA.

550
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:32,920
I've already shown you that.

551
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:34,200
You get coarctation

552
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,820
that lies distal to the arch

553
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:37,400
but proximal to the PDA,

554
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:39,720
so in between the aortic arch

555
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:40,800
and its major branches

556
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:42,340
but before the PDA.

557
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:43,420
And it presents

558
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:44,860
with lower extremity cyanosis

559
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:45,820
and high yield.

560
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:46,660
It's associated

561
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:47,720
with Turner syndrome.

562
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:49,420
Now there is another form

563
00:14:49,420 --> 00:14:50,120
of coarctation

564
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,160
called the adult form.

565
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:52,840
This is not associated

566
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:53,600
with the PDA.

567
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:54,920
You simply just get

568
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:55,820
this coarctation

569
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:56,800
that lies distal

570
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:57,820
to the aortic arch.

571
00:14:58,160 --> 00:14:59,080
And so let's just quickly

572
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:00,000
illustrate what this

573
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:00,580
would look like.

574
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:01,120
And again,

575
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,260
you've got a right atrium

576
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:03,400
and a right ventricle,

577
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:04,480
left atrium

578
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:05,580
and a left ventricle,

579
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:07,420
and here is the aorta

580
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:08,020
coming off.

581
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:09,200
These are the major branches

582
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:09,780
coming off.

583
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:10,720
And then finally,

584
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:11,840
you've got the coarctation

585
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:12,440
right here.

586
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:13,720
Now when you've got

587
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:14,660
the coarctation here,

588
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:15,280
right atrium

589
00:15:15,280 --> 00:15:16,020
to right ventricle,

590
00:15:16,060 --> 00:15:16,640
no problem.

591
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:17,780
You'll come around,

592
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:18,640
left atrium

593
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:19,360
to left ventricle,

594
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:19,940
no problem.

595
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:21,220
From the left ventricle,

596
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:21,840
there's going to be

597
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:22,520
a block here,

598
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:23,480
so you're going to put

599
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:24,940
extra blood going this way

600
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:25,860
because of that block.

601
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,220
So that's going to create

602
00:15:27,220 --> 00:15:28,060
hypertension

603
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:30,220
in the upper extremities

604
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:31,520
and it's going to create

605
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:32,700
hypotension

606
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:35,060
in the lower extremities.

607
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:36,880
And so that's the key finding

608
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:38,080
in the adult form.

609
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:38,920
Well, let's go ahead

610
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:39,560
and read what we say

611
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:40,040
in the text.

612
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:41,320
We say it presents as

613
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:43,140
hypertension in the upper extremities

614
00:15:43,140 --> 00:15:45,020
and hypotension with weak pulses

615
00:15:45,020 --> 00:15:46,040
in the lower extremity.

616
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:47,460
It's classically discovered

617
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:48,080
in adulthood

618
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:49,200
and high yield,

619
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:49,980
it's associated

620
00:15:49,980 --> 00:15:51,740
with a bicuspid aortic valve

621
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:52,940
and you're going to understand

622
00:15:52,940 --> 00:15:53,660
the consequences

623
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:55,020
of bicuspid aortic valve

624
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:56,240
in the next section

625
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:56,980
when we talk about

626
00:15:56,980 --> 00:15:58,000
valvular disorders.

627
00:15:58,660 --> 00:15:59,980
Now one of the very high yield

628
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:01,540
associations with this disorder

629
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:03,500
is that collateral circulation

630
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:04,480
will develop across

631
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:05,840
the intercostal arteries

632
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,140
in order to try

633
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:08,420
to bypass that block

634
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:09,840
and so that will result

635
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:10,780
in engorged arteries

636
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:11,580
causing notching

637
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:12,100
of the ribs.

638
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:13,140
Let me illustrate this

639
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:13,700
because it's

640
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,080
particularly high yield.

641
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:16,060
So again,

642
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:16,660
let's go back

643
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:17,560
and just quickly draw

644
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,460
the simple anatomy.

645
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:19,460
You're well aware

646
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:20,160
of the fact

647
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:21,340
that this is the right atrium,

648
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:22,120
right ventricle,

649
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:22,780
left atrium,

650
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:23,560
and left ventricle

651
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,820
and here of course

652
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:25,660
is where you've got

653
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:26,920
your coartation.

654
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:28,320
Now because there's going

655
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,660
to be increased pressure

656
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:30,280
over here,

657
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:31,440
there's going to develop

658
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:32,880
some collateral circulations

659
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:33,560
that will come

660
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:35,040
and try to deliver blood

661
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:35,800
beyond the block.

662
00:16:36,180 --> 00:16:37,000
One of those collateral

663
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,200
circulations will run

664
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,320
along the surface

665
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:39,840
of the ribs.

666
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:40,620
Remember that the

667
00:16:40,620 --> 00:16:41,660
intercostal arteries

668
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:42,740
run right along

669
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:43,540
the lower surface

670
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:44,120
of the ribs.

671
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,940
Now as those become

672
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:46,800
engorged,

673
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:48,000
they are going to

674
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,840
compress the surface

675
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:50,540
of the bone

676
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:51,360
and they're going to

677
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:52,120
cause notching

678
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,380
of the surface of the bone

679
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:54,520
and that's a very

680
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:55,600
high yield association.

681
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:57,300
Now here's a picture

682
00:16:57,300 --> 00:16:58,000
of that notching

683
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:58,620
and you can see

684
00:16:58,620 --> 00:16:59,220
so imagine

685
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:00,420
the vessels running here

686
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:01,260
because there's

687
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:02,340
engorgement of the vessel

688
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:03,320
it's going to notch

689
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:04,100
against the ribs

690
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:05,160
and so you can see

691
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:06,100
all these notching

692
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:06,700
of the ribs

693
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:07,760
where the blood vessels

694
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:08,280
are running.

695
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:09,780
Again that's a particularly

696
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:10,800
high yield association

697
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:12,400
with the adult form

698
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,520
of coartation

699
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:14,240
of the aorta

700
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:15,460
and that concludes

701
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:15,920
our section

702
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,140
on congenital disorders.

